WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.800
Modernization is a long run of changes,

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.238
and change is exactly when
telemetry goes quiet.

3
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:10.875
New resources can be born silent
unless policy forces them to emit.

4
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:14.000
Older ones only get fixed when
someone runs the cleanup.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.413
Retired resources leave
stale settings behind.

6
00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:22.525
And the security console itself is
moving to a new portal by March 2027.

7
00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:25.262
The lesson is to check flow, not settings.

8
00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:29.025
A setting that saved without error
doesn't prove anything arrived.

9
00:00:29.025 --> 00:00:33.997
So the decision: platform owners keep
every plane emitting through each change,

10
00:00:33.997 --> 00:00:36.935
security engineering
checks freshness daily,

11
00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:40.475
and an unexplained loss of logs
is treated as an incident.

12
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.340
Next, the SIEM decision.
